IMPORT prelude

-- Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 (Singapore) -- what counts as contempt of court for an ordinary person or
-- business: scandalising the court and prejudicing pending proceedings (s 3(1)(a), (b), (2) to (5), Explanation 1) with their
-- defences (ss 14, 16 to 20); abusive litigation (s 3(1)(da), (db), inserted wef 28 January 2025); disobeying orders and
-- undertakings and the aggrieved party's waiver (ss 4, 21); recording court proceedings (ss 5, 21A); online publications
-- accessed in Singapore (s 11(2)); the maximum punishments (s 12(1)) and the non-publication offence (s 13(5)); the
-- Attorney-General's consent (s 30); and the start date (s 35(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 28/1/2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/AJPA2016.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the text, the latest being Act 45 of 2024 wef 28/01/2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0050 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the conduct that makes someone a contemnor, the defences, and the maximum punishment. Not encoded:
-- corporate and partnership attribution (ss 6, 7) beyond a note, the common law and inherent powers (ss 8, 9), the jurisdiction
-- of each court (s 10), the Attorney-General's non-publication direction procedure (s 13 beyond its offence), police
-- investigation (ss 22 to 24 and the Schedule), procedure, video links, bail, appeals and enforcement of fines (ss 25 to 27,
-- 31 to 33), the third-party abuse limbs (s 3(7)) and court-ordered postponement of reports (s 14(4)).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 -- contempt`

§§ `3(1)(a), (b), (2) to (5) and ss 14, 16 to 20 -- publications`

-- s 3(1)(a): a person who "scandalises the court by intentionally publishing any matter or doing any act that (i) imputes improper
-- motives to or impugns the integrity, propriety or impartiality of any court; and (ii) poses a risk that public confidence in the
-- administration of justice would be undermined" commits contempt. (2): guilty "even if he or she did not intend to scandalise
-- the court". Explanation 1: "Fair criticism of a court is not contempt by scandalising the court".
-- s 3(1)(b): intentionally publishing matter that prejudges an issue in, or "poses a real risk of prejudice to or interference
-- with", a pending court proceeding. (3): guilty even without intending those consequences. (4): a statement "on behalf of the
-- Government" about a pending proceeding is not contempt under (1)(b) "if the Government believes that the statement is necessary
-- in the public interest" -- the exemption does not reach (1)(a).
-- Defences, each limited to the limbs named: s 14(1) good-faith fair and accurate report of a public hearing published
-- contemporaneously or within a reasonable time -- (a) and (b); s 16 good-faith report to the Chief Justice, police or other
-- authority alleging misconduct or corruption by a judge, disclosing grounds sufficient for investigation -- (a) only; s 17(1)
-- filing in good faith any action, pleading, application or affidavit in court -- (a) only; s 18 a non-author who published or
-- distributed without authority, consent or knowledge and without want of due care -- (a) and (b); s 19 publishing outside
-- Singapore without reason to believe the public in Singapore would see or hear it -- (a) and (b); s 20 no knowledge and no
-- reason to believe the proceedings were pending -- (b) only.
-- s 28: contempt must be proved beyond reasonable doubt; s 29: the burden of proving a Part 4 defence is "upon the person relying
-- on the defence", on the balance of probabilities. (Burdens are not modelled: a defence flag set TRUE means it was proved.)
DECLARE Publication HAS
    `was published intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imputes improper motives or impugns the court's integrity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `poses a risk to public confidence in the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is fair criticism` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prejudges or risks prejudice to a pending proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a Government statement believed necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a good-faith fair and accurate report of a public hearing in reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a good-faith report to the authorities with grounds for investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a good-faith court filing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was by a non-author without knowledge and with due care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was abroad with no reason to believe Singapore would see it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the publisher had no reason to believe proceedings were pending` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication scandalises the court` IF
        `the publication`'s `was published intentionally`
    AND `the publication`'s `imputes improper motives or impugns the court's integrity`
    AND `the publication`'s `poses a risk to public confidence in the administration of justice`
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is fair criticism`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is a good-faith fair and accurate report of a public hearing in reasonable time`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is a good-faith report to the authorities with grounds for investigation`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is a good-faith court filing`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `was by a non-author without knowledge and with due care`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `was abroad with no reason to believe Singapore would see it`)

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication prejudices pending proceedings` IF
        `the publication`'s `was published intentionally`
    AND `the publication`'s `prejudges or risks prejudice to a pending proceeding`
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is a Government statement believed necessary in the public interest`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `is a good-faith fair and accurate report of a public hearing in reasonable time`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `was by a non-author without knowledge and with due care`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `was abroad with no reason to believe Singapore would see it`)
    AND (NOT `the publication`'s `the publisher had no reason to believe proceedings were pending`)

§§ `11(2) -- online publications`

-- s 11(2): where the publication "was published through the Internet or other electronic media (regardless of whether it was first
-- published in Singapore or elsewhere), the publication is taken to be published in Singapore if it was accessed by members of the
-- public in Singapore". (3): any other publication, if it was published in Singapore.
GIVEN `published online` IS A BOOLEAN, `accessed by the public in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `physically published in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication is taken to be published in Singapore` IF
        (`published online` AND `accessed by the public in Singapore`)
    OR  `physically published in Singapore`

§§ `3(1)(da), (db) -- abusive litigation (wef 28 January 2025)`

-- (da): a party or advocate who conducts or commences a court proceeding and "knows or ought to know" that it "(i) involves a
-- deception on the court, or is fictitious or constitutes a mere sham; or (ii) is manifestly groundless or without foundation, and
-- involves the process of the court being employed for some ulterior or improper purpose". (db): "multiple or successive court
-- proceedings" that the person knows or ought to know are "manifestly groundless or without foundation" -- no improper purpose is
-- needed. A single groundless proceeding brought for a proper purpose is neither. Each flag below means the person knew or ought to
-- have known it.
GIVEN `a deception, fiction or sham` IS A BOOLEAN, `manifestly groundless` IS A BOOLEAN, `for an ulterior or improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `one of multiple or successive proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the litigation is contempt` IF
        `a deception, fiction or sham`
    OR  (`manifestly groundless` AND `for an ulterior or improper purpose`)
    OR  (`manifestly groundless` AND `one of multiple or successive proceedings`)

§§ `4 and 21 -- disobedience and the aggrieved party's waiver`

-- s 4(1): intentionally disobeying "any judgment, decree, direction, order, writ or other process of a court" or intentionally
-- breaching "any undertaking given to a court" (including an implied undertaking, (9)). (2): intentional disposal of property
-- subject to an enforcement order for attachment of a debt. (3): a person legally bound who intentionally omits to produce a
-- document, refuses the oath or affirmation, refuses to answer the court's question, or refuses to sign a statement.
-- (4): contempt under (1) or (2) "may be waived by the aggrieved party and such waiver relieves from liability"; (5) the court may
-- disallow the waiver if the Attorney-General has authorised investigations, proceedings have been commenced, the contempt
-- interferes with the administration of justice, or waiver would be contrary to the public interest; (7) contempt under (3) "may
-- not be waived". (9): an "aggrieved party" is a party for whose benefit the order or undertaking was made "in proceedings other
-- than a proceeding against a person in respect of any offence" -- so (a reading) no one can waive a breach in criminal
-- proceedings.
-- s 21: not guilty under s 4(1), (2) or (3) if the failure "was wholly or substantially attributable to an honest and reasonable
-- failure ... to understand an obligation" and the person "ought fairly to be excused".
DECLARE Disobedience IS ONE OF
    `breaching a court order`
    `breaching an undertaking to the court`
    `disposing of property under an attachment order`
    `withholding a document the court requires`
    `refusing the oath or affirmation`
    `refusing to answer the court's question`
    `refusing to sign a statement`

GIVEN `the disobedience` IS A Disobedience
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aggrieved party may waive it` IF
    CONSIDER `the disobedience`
    WHEN `breaching a court order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breaching an undertaking to the court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disposing of property under an attachment order` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `investigation authorised by the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `contempt proceedings commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `interferes with the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN, `waiver contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may disallow the waiver` IF
        `investigation authorised by the Attorney-General`
    OR  `contempt proceedings commenced`
    OR  `interferes with the administration of justice`
    OR  `waiver contrary to the public interest`

GIVEN `the disobedience` IS A Disobedience, `it was intentional` IS A BOOLEAN, `an honest and reasonable misunderstanding` IS A BOOLEAN, `in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN, `the aggrieved party waived it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court disallowed the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable for disobedience` IF
        `it was intentional`
    AND (NOT `an honest and reasonable misunderstanding`)
    AND NOT (    `the aggrieved party may waive it` `the disobedience`
             AND (NOT `in criminal proceedings`)
             AND `the aggrieved party waived it`
             AND (NOT `the court disallowed the waiver`))

§§ `5 and 21A -- recording court proceedings`

-- s 5(1): contempt (a) to use in court, or bring into court for recording, any recording instrument "without the permission of the
-- court"; (aa) to make a recording of court proceedings "without the permission of the court"; (b) "to publish or transmit" such a
-- recording -- with NO permission proviso; (c) to use a recording in breach of the conditions of permission. (4): the section
-- "does not apply to the making or use of audio or visual recordings ... for purposes of official transcripts of proceedings or any
-- other purpose authorised by the court". (5): recordings of online hearings and of the participants or viewers are included.
-- s 21A: not guilty under (aa), (b) or (c) where the proceeding was "conducted through an electronic means of communication" and the
-- person "did not know, and could not reasonably have known" that it was a recording of a court proceeding.
-- So permission to record does not by itself license publishing the recording: publication must itself be a purpose the court
-- authorised. (A reading of (b) with (4).)
DECLARE `Recording act` IS ONE OF
    `bringing a recorder into court to record`
    `making a recording of the hearing`
    `publishing or transmitting the recording`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Recording act`, `the court permitted the recording` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a purpose the court authorised` IS A BOOLEAN, `an online hearing the person could not have known was being recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recording act is contempt` IF
        (NOT `for a purpose the court authorised`)
    AND CONSIDER `the act`
        WHEN `bringing a recorder into court to record` THEN NOT `the court permitted the recording`
        WHEN `making a recording of the hearing` THEN (NOT `the court permitted the recording`) AND (NOT `an online hearing the person could not have known was being recorded`)
        WHEN `publishing or transmitting the recording` THEN NOT `an online hearing the person could not have known was being recorded`

§§ `12(1) and 13(5) -- maximum punishment`

-- s 12(1): (a) where the General Division of the High Court, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal punishes, "a fine not
-- exceeding $100,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or ... both"; (b) where the General Division punishes
-- contempt "in the face of or in connection with any proceedings in a State Court, Family Court or Youth Court", $20,000 or 12
-- months; (c) any other court, $20,000 or 12 months.
-- (2) the court may refuse to hear the contemnor until the contempt is purged; (3) may order a published apology; (5) may
-- discharge or remit on purging, submission or apology; (6) may convict in absence. Not modelled.
-- s 13(5): failing "without reasonable excuse" to comply with an Attorney-General's non-publication direction is an offence, "a
-- fine not exceeding $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `the Appellate Division of the High Court`
    `the Court of Appeal`
    `a State Court`
    `a Family Court`
    `a Youth Court`

GIVEN `the court` IS A Court, `contempt relates to a lower court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the higher maximum applies` IF
        (NOT `contempt relates to a lower court`)
    AND CONSIDER `the court`
        WHEN `the General Division of the High Court` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Appellate Division of the High Court` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Court of Appeal` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the court` IS A Court, `contempt relates to a lower court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the higher maximum applies` `the court` `contempt relates to a lower court` THEN 100000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `the court` IS A Court, `contempt relates to a lower court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the higher maximum applies` `the court` `contempt relates to a lower court` THEN 36 ELSE 12

GIVEN `served with a direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ignoring a non-publication direction is an offence` IF
    `served with a direction` AND (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `30 -- the Attorney-General's consent`

-- s 30(1): "No proceedings for contempt of court as defined in section 3 or 4(8) may be instituted except by or with the consent of
-- the Attorney-General." (2): not needed for contempt in the face of the court under s 25, or for proceedings the General Division,
-- the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal commences on its own motion. s 4(8) is a non-party who causes or abets a breach of
-- an order. So a party enforcing its own order against the other party (s 4(1)) needs no consent.
GIVEN `under section 3 or 4(8)` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the face of the court` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the superior court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Attorney-General's consent is needed` IF
        `under section 3 or 4(8)`
    AND (NOT `in the face of the court`)
    AND (NOT `on the superior court's own motion`)

§§ `35(1) -- start date`

-- s 35(1): "This Act does not apply to any act of contempt of court committed before 1 October 2017." The date is written as a
-- number YYYYMMDD. (Whether the 2025 abuse limbs reach earlier conduct is not said in the text; not modelled.)
GIVEN `date as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to contempt committed on` IF
    `date as YYYYMMDD` AT LEAST 20171001
